FFmpeg master 8876f61947bf (2026-11-07), not in 9.1:
https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/commit/8876f61947bf922e6e30c1c2df83fd7f55759b9a

The AAC encoder (aac: the conversions of the sites, -acodec aac): when the rate
loop encoded a frame again, it restored the coefficients of each element by the
type of the last element, not of the element restored; for layouts that do not
end in a channel pair (4.0, 5.1, 6.1, 7.1: a 5.1 upload converted without -ac 2)
the second channel of each pair was encoded from coefficients already filtered:
wrong sound. fix-aacenc-2 to -4 apply after this one.

diff --git a/libavcodec/aacenc.c b/libavcodec/aacenc.c
index 5b1e3eff..50a1460e 100644
--- a/libavcodec/aacenc.c
+++ b/libavcodec/aacenc.c
@@ -1650,7 +1650,7 @@ static int aac_encode_frame(AVCodecContext *avctx, AVPacket *avpkt,
                 if (is_mode || ms_mode || tns_mode || pred_mode) {
                     for (i = 0; i < s->chan_map[0]; i++) {
                         // Must restore coeffs
-                        chans = tag == TYPE_CPE ? 2 : 1;
+                        chans = s->chan_map[i + 1] == TYPE_CPE ? 2 : 1;
                         cpe = &s->cpe[i];
                         for (ch = 0; ch < chans; ch++)
                             memcpy(cpe->ch[ch].coeffs, cpe->ch[ch].pcoeffs, sizeof(cpe->ch[ch].coeffs));
